# =============================================================================
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (tools/tsan.supp)
#
# Purpose
# -------
# The Qt 6 GUI smoke tests run a real Qt event loop / windowing stack under
# ThreadSanitizer.  Qt's own internals (implicitly-shared QArrayData, the
# QThreadPool, QWidget event dispatch, QWidget destruction) generate data-race
# reports whose stack frames are entirely inside libQt6*.  These are Qt's
# internal synchronization, not neko-browser code.
#
# These suppressions are scoped STRICTLY to Qt library modules.  No neko
# source file is suppressed here: a race whose top frame is inside
# src/, tests/ or any project target will still be reported and must be fixed.
#
# Verified 2026-08: every suppressed report had only libQt6* frames on both
# the read and the write side.
# =============================================================================

race:libQt6Core.so*
race:libQt6Gui.so*
race:libQt6Widgets.so*
